WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
GitHub Actions.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.447
For anything hosted on GitHub, reading and writing a workflow file is simply assumed.

3
00:00:07.447 --> 00:00:08.867
Let's learn the pieces.

4
00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:16.367
A workflow is CI CD written as YAML, stored in your repo under dot github slash workflows.

5
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:20.100
It names its triggers, its jobs, and the steps inside them.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.343
Secrets are injected from repo settings and never committed.

7
00:00:24.343 --> 00:00:27.300
And a matrix can fan one job across versions.

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.900
Three layers to remember.

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.133
Triggers decide when it runs: a push, a tag, a pull request, or a schedule.

10
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:39.133
Jobs each run on a fresh runner machine, and needs puts them in order.

11
00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:44.967
Steps are shell commands, plus prebuilt marketplace actions, so you compose rather than script.

12
00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.067
Here is the pipeline from the page.

13
00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:51.000
A push to main, or a version tag, triggers it.

14
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.667
The test job runs the linter and the tests.

15
00:00:53.967 --> 00:00:58.267
The image job needs the test job to pass, so a failure stops everything.

16
00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.867
And only a version tag actually pushes to the registry.

17
00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.300
And the file itself.

18
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.900
The trigger is a push to main, or any tag starting with v.

19
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.867
The test job checks out the code, installs dependencies, and runs the tests.

20
00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:17.767
The image job needs the test job, and runs only when the ref is a version tag.

21
00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:20.767
Here is a senior-level habit.

22
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.095
Add a third job.

23
00:01:22.095 --> 00:01:27.367
After the unit tests pass, it runs RAGAS over the twenty five question golden set.

24
00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:31.767
If faithfulness drops below zero point eight five, the job fails.

25
00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.998
The pull request cannot merge.

26
00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:39.533
Evals as a merge gate is exactly what the market calls senior as of twenty twenty-six.

27
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:41.515
Let's recap.

28
00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:43.600
Workflows are YAML in your repo.

29
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.200
They are made of triggers, jobs and steps.

30
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.633
Needs makes each job gate the next.

31
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:52.006
And evals as a merge gate is a senior habit.

32
00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:53.333
Next up: Terraform.
